    "body": "EICMA 2026 • Yamaha Births New Adventure Scooter Family, Three RW Models That Look More Like Motorcycles\nMG Motor Treats Australia to a Special Edition of the Successful MG4 EV Urban All-Electric Hatchback\n28 photos\nPhoto: MG Motor Australia\nMG Motor Australia is giving its popular MG4 EV Urban a fresh makeover with the MG4 EV Urban Special Edition, priced at AU $33,990, including a $2,000 cashback offer on the drive-away price. That’s just a little more than $23k, which isn't bad at all.\nMG was established in England in 1924, and more than a century later Morris Garages has gained a new lease of life thanks to the Chinese automotive manufacturer SAIC Motor. Currently, “MG offers a broad range of vehicles to suit all needs, including battery electric , advanced hybrid, petrol and diesel, making the latest automotive technologies more accessible than ever.” To support its affordability claims, here’s the latest version of one of their accessible EV models, ready for primetime in Australia.\nMG Motor launched the MG4 EV, or MG4 Electric, as an all-electric small family car (C-segment) in the summer of 2022 at home in China. It quickly traveled that year to the Old Continent and other markets, helping “make EV ownership more affordable, practical and enjoyable for everyday drivers,” according to the company. Last year, MG launched a second version, called MG4 EV Urban, based on the newer SAIC E3 electric vehicle architecture using a cell-to-body battery design and featuring FWD only.\nNow, MG Motor Australia is refreshing the MG4 EV Urban with a limited-edition model, “bringing exclusive styling enhancements and added interior ambience to one of Australia’s most accessible electric vehicles.” It comes with exclusive features like a contrasting, black-painted roof, black exterior mirrors, ambient lighting integrated into the door panels, and an all-new Ice Blue metallic exterior paint color, among other things.\nThe special edition will have Ice Blue and the existing Diamond Red as the exclusive two-color offerings. It’s available now for purchase through MG dealerships nationwide, and the Special Edition costs AU $1k more than the entry-level MG4 EV Urban Essence 54. The Special Edition retains the Essence 54 specification and comes with the larger 54kWh battery configuration, enough for a range of up to 405 km (WLTP) or 252 miles.\nIt also has DC fast charging from 10 to 80 percent in approximately 30 minutes, seating for five, 382 liters (13.49 cu-ft) for the luggage compartment and an additional 98 liters (3.46 cu-ft) under the boot, Front Wheel Drive, as well as a five-star ANCAP safety rating. All MG4 EV Urban models have a 10-year warranty when serviced within MG’s national dealer network.\n“The MG4 EV Urban has proven to be a popular choice with Australian buyers, and we think this Special Edition will build on that appeal. It’s already a great car, so we’ve added a few distinctive touches to make it even more appealing. The Special Edition will be limited to just 750 units in Australia, and we’re excited to see customers get behind it,” said Dimitri Andreatidis, Marketing Director at MG Motor Australia.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nMG4 EV Urban Special Edition MG4 EV Urban MG Motor MG 4 EV Urban EV pricing Australia\nAbout the author: Aurel Niculescu\nAurel has aimed high all his life (literally, at 16 he was flying gliders all by himself) so in 2006 he switched careers and got hired as a writer at his favorite magazine. Since then, his work has been published both by print and online outlets, most recently right here, on autoevolution. Full profile\nUP NEXT Renault Forefront Is a Cabinless Remote-Controlled Robotic Truck Meant for the Military",
